<title>UK: House of Fraser up, report raises bid hopes.</title>
<headline>House of Fraser up, report raises bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in House of Fraser Plc rose in early trading on Friday after a report in the Daily Mail newspaper raised the possibility the department store group could be the target of a takeover bid.</p>
<p>The stock was up 5p at 162 by 0740 GMT, after yesterday tumbling as low as 153p -- its lowest since January.</p>
<p>The stock was floated at 180p in May 1994.  </p>
<p>The report said there was talk in the market that the company could be target of a bid and that an unnamed buyer had been accumulating stock.</p>
</text>
